From: Markus Theil <markus.theil@tu-ilmenau.de>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:34:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: Set HANDLE_DFS for the channel switch of a mesh

nl80211_channel_switch() rejects with -EINVAL a channel switch to a
channel that requires DFS, unless NL80211_ATTR_HANDLE_DFS is set; only
AP and P2P GO interfaces are exempt. wpa_supplicant sets the flag for
the mesh join only. A mesh that wpa_supplicant runs on a DFS channel
thus cannot switch to another DFS channel, with CHAN_SWITCH or after a
radar detection.

Set the flag for the channel switch if the mesh join set it, that is if
wpa_supplicant handles DFS for the mesh. A mesh that joined without it
does not handle radar events and keeps the rejection, as mac80211 does
for the channel switch of a mesh peer
(ieee80211_mesh_process_chnswitch()).

Signed-off-by: Markus Theil <markus.theil@tu-ilmenau.de>
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -12380,6 +12380,8 @@ static int nl80211_switch_channel(void *
 	    (ret = nl80211_put_freq_params(msg, &settings->freq_params, bss)) ||
 	    (settings->block_tx &&
 	     nla_put_flag(msg, NL80211_ATTR_CH_SWITCH_BLOCK_TX)) ||
+	    (drv->nlmode == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT && drv->mesh_handle_dfs &&
+	     nla_put_flag(msg, NL80211_ATTR_HANDLE_DFS)) ||
 	    (settings->link_id != NL80211_DRV_LINK_ID_NA &&
 	     nla_put_u8(msg, NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINK_ID, settings->link_id)))
 		goto error;
@@ -13174,6 +13176,7 @@ static int nl80211_join_mesh(struct i802
 	}
 	ret = 0;
 	drv->assoc_freq = bss->flink->freq = params->freq.freq;
+	drv->mesh_handle_dfs = params->handle_dfs;
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "nl80211: mesh join request sent successfully");
 
 fail:
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.h
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.h
@@ -221,6 +221,7 @@ struct wpa_driver_nl80211_data {
 	unsigned int qca_ap_allowed_freqs:1;
 	unsigned int connect_ext_vendor_cmd_avail:1;
 	unsigned int support_ap_scan:1;
+	unsigned int mesh_handle_dfs:1;
 
 	u8 extra_bss_membership_selectors[8];
 
